        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Mix of run-of-river hydropower plants built between 1945 and 1980, representative for Europe. Capacity: 8.6MW.\n\n# Included processes\nThe dataset includes the most important materials used for the construction of an average run-of-river hydropower plant: cement, gravel, water, steel, copper and explosives. Furthermore, transports, the energy used, particle emissions and disposal/recycling of the materials are included.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
